  "body": "Hello lovely humans,\n\n[preact](https://www.npmjs.com/package/preact) just published its new version 6.0.1.\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      State\n    </th>\n    <td>\n      Update :rocket:\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      Dependency\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      preact\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      New version\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      6.0.1\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <th align=left>\n      Type\n    </td>\n    <td>\n      devDependency\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\nThis version is **not covered** by your **current version range**.\n\nWithout accepting this pull request your project will work just like it did before. There might be a bunch of new features, fixes and perf improvements that the maintainers worked on for you though.\n\nI recommend you look into these changes and try to get onto the latest version of preact.\nGiven that you have a decent test suite, a passing build is a strong indicator that you can take advantage of these changes by merging the proposed change into your project. Otherwise this branch is a great starting point for you to work on the update.\n\nDo you have any ideas how I could improve these pull requests? Did I report anything you think isn’t right?\nAre you unsure about how things are supposed to work?\n\nThere is a collection of [frequently asked questions](https://greenkeeper.io/faq.html) and while I’m just a bot, there is a group of people who are happy to teach me new things. [Let them know](https://github.com/greenkeeperio/greenkeeper/issues/new).\n\nGood luck with your project :sparkles:\n\nYou rock!\n\n:palm_tree:\n\n---\n\nThe new version differs by 27 commits .\n- [`d26ab44`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/d26ab44ac21a85650e22cf0dc3d8efc28997a569) <code>6.0.1</code>\n- [`d3c7a46`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/d3c7a46d0702b00d9fbb2171ae86fcb6ae60d606) <code>Install missing dependency for npm t (#291)</code>\n- [`81c5808`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/81c5808dc1be53c60a0a02ff1022060cedae0d60) <code>chore(package): update pretty-bytes-cli to version 2.0.0 (#285)</code>\n- [`23f6c44`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/23f6c4428e0b2d9f19888e6a1a0c0a214ad7562b) <code>6.0.0</code>\n- [`6be3ff5`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/6be3ff501982017b173b43dba9be6d60451c0b17) <code>Follow-up to #260: When picking up from SSR, no elements are marked with `_component`/`_componentConstructor` and thus none match via `isSameNodeType()`. When this happens, fall back to attempting to re-use elements in-order.</code>\n- [`5c22af6`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/5c22af6ea467d89fd0f95efaf944a4c4c1e7b5fa) <code>Amendment to solution for #260: when in `mountAll` mode (initial render of a component), attempt to re-use parent's `base` for high-order children that do not initialize with a recycled `base`.</code>\n- [`ceb6167`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/ceb6167568286aba1188f2e933ff1c403a0c630a) <code>Breaking: Discard keyed nodes when they don't match the updated DOM description instead of allowing them to be re-used unkeyed. This should fix #254 /cc @gnaeus</code>\n- [`cfe02d4`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/cfe02d48830fd665aa1db5037183b4223409559c) <code>✄ (Small) Breaking Change: `linkState()` no longer falls back to component paths and no longer auto-invokes the target path if it is a function.  These features were unused and poor documented, and added extra weight.</code>\n- [`ba48cd3`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/ba48cd3741bb1266dab6418db19783aa151c182b) <code>Fix flakey test relying on attribute ordering in `innerHTML` serialization (Firefox 45 I'm looking at you)</code>\n- [`4da16e2`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/4da16e209dca0f3b75bd94db9ad321a4698b274e) <code>Bugfix: when swapping between Text, Comment and Element nodes, reclaim whole orphaned trees rather than just their roots.</code>\n- [`7049c08`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/7049c0851d8737069ea632298a8ac9ed89aea05f) <code>Bugfix: prevent the recycler from collecting non-Element nodes 🐛</code>\n- [`68dce67`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/68dce67f2c17a419320e2dfa59673dce3dffcbfc) <code>Remove default empty `vnode` hook (note: this is technically a breaking change, but very few people use this API and documentation has mentioned performing an existence check on the previous hook prior to calling it for a long time)</code>\n- [`513ba51`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/513ba510fc72245f2e5df1e51f5ab66618108d58) <code>Remove commented out code.</code>\n- [`1ba8ef7`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/1ba8ef7a767e34db3a0aa949d4053a3a2f8e015d) <code>Add inline doc/note about VNode Hooks as suggested by @Robert-Wett 👍</code>\n- [`4fc4a85`](https://github.com/developit/preact/commit/4fc4a851aeb853c4fa2050e956a61453864bd069) <code>Merge branch 'master' of github.com:developit/preact</code>\n\nThere are 27 commits in total. See the [full diff](https://github.com/developit/preact/compare/a495b9d283c48abae911c175beaf07c62f8e8401...d26ab44ac21a85650e22cf0dc3d8efc28997a569).\n\n---\n\nThis pull request was created by [greenkeeper.io](https://greenkeeper.io/).\n\n<sub>Tired of seeing this sponsor message? :zap: `greenkeeper upgrade`</sub>\n",
